1. Addison's Disease: Hyposecretion of adrenal cortex (glucocorticoids & aldosterone);
Symptoms: Severe hypoglycemia, hyponatremia, hyperkalemia, acute weakness, hypotension, and characteristic bronze skin pigmentation.
2. Cushing's Syndrome: Hypersecretion of cortisol (often due to adrenal tumor);
Symptoms: Hyperglycemia, hypertension, breakdown of muscle proteins, 'Moon face', 'Buffalo hump' fat accumulation on upper back, and osteoporosis.
